eatine plays a key role in cognitive function, helping to boost intelligence, reasoning, and short-term memory. It also supports brain resilience by reducing the severity of trauma and accelerating recovery after injury.</p><br><p>Beyond cognition, creatine can help improve your mental response to stress, keeping your mind sharper and more adaptable under pressure. It’s even been shown to support mood and may help ease symptoms of depression.</p><br><p>Fuel your body&nbsp;<em>and</em>&nbsp;your brain with the power of creatine.</p></span></div></div><picture data-rid="55902566-6e20-42c0-bc55-224cb51fa941" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-pdu7oo"><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Brain_Benefits_SingleServe_Beige-min.png?v=1740771722&amp;width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Brain_Benefits_SingleServe_Beige-min.png?v=1740771722&amp;width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Brain_Benefits_SingleServe_Beige-min.png?v=1740771722&amp;width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Brain_Benefits_SingleServe_Beige-min.png?v=1740771722" alt="Image listing key brain benefits of creatine, accompanied by creatine supplement packages." class="r-9hgobb" loading="eager"/></picture></div><div data-rid="3e27f04a-39eb-4fa1-94cf-0a62efc2667b" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0" class="r-kgqquc"><div data-rid="6e1627a1-7904-466f-8dba-892d6e06388e" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-11tynv4"><picture data-rid="cd558262-95d6-42cf-ba41-0a0f71fd82ab" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-1n6bqx"><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Screenshot_2025-02-28_at_2.47.40_PM.png?v=1740772080&amp;width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Screenshot_2025-02-28_at_2.47.40_PM.png?v=1740772080&amp;width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Screenshot_2025-02-28_at_2.47.40_PM.png?v=1740772080&amp;width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Screenshot_2025-02-28_at_2.47.40_PM.png?v=1740772080" alt="Image explaining negative effects of missing one week of creatine supplementation." class="r-or1ok3" loading="eager"/></picture></div><div data-rid="1d479a8b-7bc9-4d91-b23a-b127d7beaf31" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-xjyrc0"><div data-rid="656f0bbc-67f5-457e-8b1d-1e7200d96972" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-kjracr alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">What Happens When You’re Not Taking Creatine?</span></p></span></div><div data-rid="351d9721-9c1c-43b3-96fb-d4f587309197" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-1b2whbf alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Missing a day or two of creatine won’t make a huge difference, but after a full week, you’ll start to feel the effects. One of the first things you might notice is increased brain fog. With lower creatine levels, neurons fire less efficiently, which can reduce focus, memory, and mental energy.</p><br><p>Your muscle endurance may also take a hit as ATP production slows down, leading to lower energy levels during workouts. At the same time, muscles can lose some of the water they’ve retained, making them appear slightly flatter. On top of that, recovery becomes slower and fatigue sets in more easily, as your body struggles to replenish muscle energy at its usual pace.</p><br><p>To keep your mind sharp, muscles full, and recovery times quick, consistency is key—don’t let your progress slip!</p></span></div></div></div><div data-rid="7b51f8fd-8d29-4748-a247-51c1c33311cd" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0" data-alchemy-url-hashmark="creapure" tabindex="-1" id="creapure" data-alchemy-url-hashmark-ignore="true" class="r-192z248"><div data-rid="7979eca3-cdec-4190-be2e-04f82d65c200" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-wkt9c"><div data-rid="842a07f1-894e-440c-b312-53a99342398f" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-1mmiwug alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p></p></span></div><div data-rid="aedb924b-6243-462b-b5fa-bcf6e88044c7" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-1mlhexa alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">Why Do Your Workouts Feel Flat and Sluggish?</span></p></span></div><div data-rid="25ed3488-e6a9-40c0-9422-391e7f502bde" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-1ye8la8 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>If your gym sessions feel like a grind and your performance has stalled, your muscles may be lacking the quick energy they need for peak performance. Creatine supercharges your muscles by boosting ATP production, giving you the extra strength, endurance, and power to break through plateaus.</p><br><p>Whether you’re lifting, sprinting, or cycling, creatine helps you hit your goals with renewed intensity. It supports all athletic endeavors and lifestyles, providing the extra boost you need to perform at your best—no matter the activity.</p><br><p>Plateauing in the gym and not seeing the rewards of your hard work is frustrating. Creatine helps you push past those limits and keeps your progress moving forward.</p></span></div></div><picture data-rid="58a780b2-d676-4107-a0a8-2cc354934b55" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-1amjhv5"><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Infographic_PercGainsvsPlacebo_BeigeBG_5809c00a-4d01-47c7-a8a9-31be65ea5709.png?v=1740784348&amp;width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Infographic_PercGainsvsPlacebo_BeigeBG_5809c00a-4d01-47c7-a8a9-31be65ea5709.png?v=1740784348&amp;width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Infographic_PercGainsvsPlacebo_BeigeBG_5809c00a-4d01-47c7-a8a9-31be65ea5709.png?v=1740784348&amp;width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Infographic_PercGainsvsPlacebo_BeigeBG_5809c00a-4d01-47c7-a8a9-31be65ea5709.png?v=1740784348" alt="Bar chart comparing creatine and placebo effects on muscle gains and side effects." class="r-12dkfjs" loading="eager"/></picture></div><div data-rid="dc541058-9fd0-46a4-a156-5bc693256f28" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0" class="r-1bnfm8s"><div data-rid="890b4797-b53b-4980-a576-55843764b7b4" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-34xfk2"><picture data-rid="8e366748-20e7-43ad-a1fc-62464cdb023d" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-12hc2fg"><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Infographic_MemoryImprovementWithCreatine_OrangeBG_f325bf68-3c93-4241-8413-16741f5cd6fb.png?v=1740784427&amp;width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Infographic_MemoryImprovementWithCreatine_OrangeBG_f325bf68-3c93-4241-8413-16741f5cd6fb.png?v=1740784427&amp;width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Infographic_MemoryImprovementWithCreatine_OrangeBG_f325bf68-3c93-4241-8413-16741f5cd6fb.png?v=1740784427&amp;width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Infographic_MemoryImprovementWithCreatine_OrangeBG_f325bf68-3c93-4241-8413-16741f5cd6fb.png?v=1740784427" alt="Bar chart showing memory improvement with creatine in younger and older adults." class="r